The Security Council,

Recalling all its previous resolutions on Lebanon, in particular resolutions 425 (1978), 426 (1978), 1559 (2004), 1701 (2006), 2695 (2023), and 2749 (2024), as well as the relevant statements of its President,

Expressing its continued deep concern at the ongoing hostilities across the Blue Line, the high number of casualties, and the risk of further regional escalation,

Reaffirming its strong commitment to the full implementation of all provisions of resolution 1701 (2006), and aware of its responsibilities to help secure a permanent ceasefire and a long-term solution as envisioned in the resolution,

Reiterating its strong support for the territorial integrity, sovereignty, and political independence of Lebanon within its internationally recognized borders, and under the sole authority of the Government of Lebanon,

Commending the United Nations Interim Force in Lebanon (UNIFIL) and its troop-contributing countries for their vital role, commitment, and dedication to peace and stability in southern Lebanon, operating under extremely challenging and perilous conditions,

Condemning all incidents affecting the safety and security of UNIFIL personnel and premises, and emphasizing the obligation of all parties to respect the security and safety of United Nations peacekeepers and property at all times,

Responding to the request of the Government of Lebanon to extend the mandate of UNIFIL for a period of one year,

1. Decides to extend the present mandate of UNIFIL until 31 August 2026;

2. Demands the full implementation of resolution 1701 (2006) by all parties, and calls for a complete cessation of hostilities and a restoration of calm across the Blue Line;

3. Strongly urges all relevant actors to implement immediate measures towards de-escalation, exercise maximum restraint, and refrain from any action that could lead to a broader conflagration;

4. Reaffirms the call on all parties to respect the Blue Line in its entirety and to cooperate fully with the United Nations and UNIFIL, including through the tripartite mechanism;

5. Urges the parties to ensure that the freedom of movement of UNIFIL in all its operations and UNIFIL’s access to the Blue Line in all its parts are fully respected and unimpeded, in accordance with its mandate and rules of engagement, and underscores that UNIFIL does not require prior authorization or permission to undertake its mandated tasks;

6. Condemns all attacks against UNIFIL peacekeepers, vehicles, installations, and premises, calls upon the Lebanese authorities to swiftly bring the perpetrators of such attacks to justice, and reminds all parties of their obligations under international humanitarian law;

7. Reaffirms the necessity of an effective and durable deployment of the Lebanese Armed Forces in southern Lebanon and calls on the international community to strengthen and expand its support to the Lebanese Armed Forces;

8. Requests the Secretary-General to continue to report to the Council on the implementation of resolution 1701 (2006) every four months, or at any time as he deems appropriate;

9. Decides to remain actively seized of the matter.

